---
import Layout from '@/components/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, EMAIL_URL, SITE_NAME } from '@/lib/site';

const title = `Cookie policy — ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description =
  'Transparent information regarding the use of cookies and local technical storage on Jull Ortiz’s website.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/cookies/">
  <main class="content-shell">
    <PageHero
      title="Cookie policy"
      eyebrow="Transparency & Privacy · Technical Local Storage"
    />

    <article class="prose mt-8 max-w-[48rem]">
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">1. What are cookies and local storage?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          Cookies and local storage mechanisms (such as <code>localStorage</code>) are small data files stored by your browser when visiting websites. Their primary purpose is to preserve user preferences and ensure essential technical functionality.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">2. What technologies do we use?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          This website is built upon privacy-by-design and data minimization principles. <strong>We do not use advertising tracking cookies or commercialize user browsing profiles.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          We solely utilize strictly necessary technical local storage:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-ink-soft">
          <li>
            <strong><code>theme-palette</code></strong>: Stores your selected color palette or visual theme (e.g., warm, high contrast, neon, or seasonal mode) to maintain aesthetic consistency across visits.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong><code>cookie-consent</code></strong>: Stores your acknowledgment of this technical storage notice, preventing repeated banner prompts.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">3. External links and services</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          This website contains external links to official and collaborative platforms, such as the Google Maps profile for <strong>SHA256.US</strong>, professional profiles on LinkedIn, repositories on GitHub, verifiable credentials on IBM SkillsBuild / Credly, and the official <strong>SUSCERTE</strong> portal.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          When clicking on external links, you leave this website. Those external platforms maintain their own independent privacy and cookie policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">4. How to manage or clear this data</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          You can inspect, block, or clear locally stored data at any time through your browser settings (under Privacy and Security / Site data).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">5. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          For any inquiries regarding this policy or technical storage practices, contact {AUTHOR_NAME} directly at: <a href={EMAIL_URL} class="font-bold underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 text-accent hover:text-ink">julljoll@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

